@startuml state-diagram
' Shipment lifecycle state machine.
' Source of truth: Domains/ShipmentStatus.allowedNext() / canTransitionTo(),
' enforced by ShipmentServiceImpl.updateStatus(); every transition records a
' TrackingEvent and publishes ShipmentStatusChangedEvent.
title Shipment Status — State Machine Diagram

hide empty description

[*] --> CREATED : createShipment()

CREATED --> PACKED
PACKED --> DISPATCHED : dispatch\n/ SalesOrderShipmentSyncListener\nupdates sales order status

DISPATCHED --> IN_TRANSIT
DISPATCHED --> EXCEPTION

IN_TRANSIT --> OUT_FOR_DELIVERY
IN_TRANSIT --> EXCEPTION

OUT_FOR_DELIVERY --> DELIVERED : record delivery
OUT_FOR_DELIVERY --> EXCEPTION

EXCEPTION --> IN_TRANSIT : resolved
EXCEPTION --> OUT_FOR_DELIVERY : retry delivery
EXCEPTION --> RETURNED : return to warehouse

DELIVERED --> [*]
RETURNED --> [*]

state CREATED : label "Created"
state PACKED : label "Packed"
state DISPATCHED : label "Dispatched"\ncountsAsShipped
state IN_TRANSIT : label "In transit"\ncountsAsShipped
state OUT_FOR_DELIVERY : label "Out for delivery"\ncountsAsShipped
state EXCEPTION : label "Delivery exception"\ncountsAsShipped
state DELIVERED : label "Delivered"\nterminal, countsAsShipped
state RETURNED : label "Returned"\nterminal

note bottom of EXCEPTION
  Any transition not listed in allowedNext()
  is rejected with InvalidShipmentStatusTransitionException.
end note
@enduml
